  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IPFCS-24HOUR TEENYEEU Model</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institute for Population, Family &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Children Studies (IPFCS) in collaboration with 3 stakeholders: Center for Children and Development (CCD), Institute for Development &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Community Health (LIGHT), and Center for Legal Consultancy and Policy Research creates a proposal in addressing issues regarding gender and sexuality understanding of children. The project aims to raise awareness for the children within Hoang Mai district, Hanoi about gender &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; sexuality knowledge and related laws by developing 6 Teenyeeu 24h Clubs operated based on the code of conduct in education institutions that will be built under the perspective of gender with the participation of students. Under the operation of the clubs, 6 camps will also be organized to connect children with their teachers, parents, and local community, opening up a space for exchange and dialog for better understanding about gender and sexuality. Furthermore, with the Institute along with other 3 project stakeholders will build up a network of collaborator/legalconsultant regarding gender and sexuality for juvenile. Last but not least, the project desires to promote the participation of children in contributing to comment on the draft of Law on Gender Equality and gender &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; sexuality communication through the development of code of conduct, online dialogue for the juvenile and manager on legal development. Overall, the expected outcomes of this initiative are developing 6 clubs related to gender and sexuality, raise awareness for 5000 students at 6 education institutions, forming a network oflegal consultancy, and establishing 6 codes of conducts in each institution.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Union</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institute for Population, Family &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Children Studies (IPFCS) &#x2013; a science and technology organization, was established on January 21st, 2013 based on the Decision No. 12/HDBT of the Government and operated based on the Decree No. 81/2002/ND-CP. It is an institute where collective scientists and specialists with experiences and passion in the area of Population, Family and Children to build and perform research, projects, and apply it to improve science and technology services in contribution to increase the quality ofpopulation, economy, culture, and society. In particular, its function is to provide services such as policy consultancy, survey, evaluation, criticism, recommendation, capacity building training, seminars,..related to the area of population,family, and children.Furthermore, the Institute collaborates closely with organizations, individuals, businesses domestically and externally to perform the above-mentioned services. Applicable to Justice Initiatives Facilitation Fund (JIFF)-Oxfam project, IPFCS has been able to show their experiences, specifically in the legal and justice filed, related to comment on Legal Draft, implement educational programme based on legal regulated documents, and provide consultation to revise laws and policies.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institute for Population, Family</narrative>
